[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5698595370","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123531#issuecomment-5698595370","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123531","id":5698595370,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABU6mqKg","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T13:51:13Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T13:51:34Z","body":"> Code itself looks good to me.\r\n> \r\n> Not the biggest fan of needing to pass a `Variant &r_tmp_variant` from the callee, but it is necessary in this new design. Since the `validate()` and `_internal_validate()` methods are only used in the `Array` and `Dictionary` classes, the additional boilerplate this results in stays small in scope, so fine by me.\r\n\r\nRight, it's a bit unusual. This \"pattern\" isn't easy to represent in C++ so that's why it ended up like this.\r\nThe main alternative I see would be a temporary \"Validator\" object that handles both. It would look like this:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nValidated validated = _p->typed.validate(p_value, \"push_back\");\r\nERR_FAIL_NULL(validated.ptr());\r\n\r\n_p->array.push_back(validated.ptr());\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhile one line shorter, the it's much harder to understand what's going on. \"Validated\" is opaque, as is `ptr()`. You have to know what it is to understand it. The code as now is much clearer in that because the types are plain and known.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5698595370/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5705245615","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123531#issuecomment-5705245615","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123531","id":5705245615,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVA8jrw","user":{"login":"aurpine","id":12262539,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjYyNTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12262539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine","html_url":"https://github.com/aurpine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T22:05:46Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T22:05:46Z","body":"Salvaging over my benchmarks. Each test is only run 6 times on `N=100,